=== THE JOHNSON DIVIDE RATIO, ESTABLISHED EXPERIMENTALLY ===
Date: 2026-11-22 ~15:35-15:45 UTC+7
Host: macOS, Digilent HS2 (FT232H 0x0403:0x6014), busdev 1:3

THE QUESTION. The R4/T4 reading of ~398.7 MHz assumed the two-stage Johnson prescaler divides
by 256. If it divides by 512, the same reading is 199.3 MHz - which would match the parent
repository's documented "200 MHz oscillator on R4/T4" EXACTLY. That factor of two had to be
settled on silicon before any clock number could be published.

THE CONTROL. The control is the MEASURED R4/T4 design with ONE thing changed: the clock comes
from STARTUPE2.CFGMCLK instead of the R4/T4 oscillator. The netlists are cell-identical apart
from the clock primitive and one output buffer:

  measured R4/T4 netlist : BSCANE2 1, BUFG 3, FDRE 63, FDSE 6, INV 2, LUT2 21, LUT3 21,
                           LUT4 19, IBUFDS 1
  control netlist        : BSCANE2 1, BUFG 3, FDRE 63, FDSE 6, INV 2, LUT2 21, LUT3 21,
                           LUT4 19, STARTUPE2 1, OBUF 1

  => the divide chain, the counter and the readback are the SAME in both. Only the clock source
     differs, plus one OBUF: the control's LED on B13, which is a TAP of an existing counter
     bit (no extra flip-flop). That package pin exists only to anchor the placer; without any
     package pin nextpnr's placer scatters the BSCANE2 shift register and the design does not
     route (verified: the port-free control failed in 40 seeds).

  The synthesis flow that reproduces the measured netlist exactly:
    synth_xilinx -family xc7 -nodsp -nosrl -nolutram -nocarry ... abc -lut 2 ...
  The -nocarry is what turns the counter's increment into LUT logic instead of a CARRY4 chain,
  which is what the measured netlist contains (CARRY4 count 0, LUT4 count 19).

